{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "f3dfd8ea-b4c6-4a61-b971-795d1d380efc",
		"name": "geo-post-api",
		"description": "Collection for the geo-post-api service (hyper-local social media backend). A single Gin service backed by Postgres (GORM) and Redis, with Zero-Trust JWT auth, plus MinIO-backed media uploads.\n\nEnvironment variables used throughout:\n- `base_url` - geo-post-api base URL, e.g. `http://localhost:8091`\n- `baseurl` - the external auth service's base URL, e.g. `http://localhost:8081`. Used only by the **Auth** folder to obtain a token for testing - geo-post-api itself never calls this at request time (Zero-Trust: it only verifies JWTs locally against JWT_PUBLIC_KEY_PATH).\n- `TOKEN` / `REFRESH_TOKEN` - set automatically by **Auth > LogIn(GetToken)**'s test script. Every request under **Protected (api/v1)** sends `Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN}}` via folder-level auth - run LogIn(GetToken) first.\n\nSee the `geo-post-api` environment file in this folder for the variable definitions.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "31158988",
		"_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/31158988-f3dfd8ea-b4c6-4a61-b971-795d1d380efc?source=collection_link"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Auth",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "LogIn(GetToken)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const response = pm.response.json();\npm.collectionVariables.set('TOKEN', response.accessToken);\npm.collectionVariables.set('REFRESH_TOKEN', response.refreshToken);\n"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "noauth"
						},
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@localhost.com\",\n  \"password\": \"admin\"\n}",
							"options": {
								"raw": {
									"language": "json"
								}
							}
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{centerurl}}/api/auth/login",
							"host": [
								"{{centerurl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"auth",
								"login"
							]
						},
						"description": "Logs into the external auth service to obtain an RS256 access token signed with the private key matching this repo's `cert/public_key.pem`. On success, the attached test script saves `accessToken` into `TOKEN` and `refreshToken` into `REFRESH_TOKEN` - every request under **Protected (api/v1)** picks up `TOKEN` immediately, no manual copy/paste needed. Run this first."
					},
					"response": [
						{
							"name": "200 OK",
							"originalRequest": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@localhost.com\",\n  \"password\": \"admin\"\n}",
									"options": {
										"raw": {
											"language": "json"
										}
									}
								},
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseurl}}/api/auth/login",
									"host": [
										"{{baseurl}}"
									],
									"path": [
										"api",
										"auth",
										"login"
									]
								}
							},
							"status": "OK",
							"code": 200,
							"_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
							"header": [
								{
									"key": "Content-Type",
									"value": "application/json"
								}
							],
							"cookie": [],
							"body": "{\n    \"accessToken\": \"eyJraWQiOiIuLi4iLCJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiJ9...\",\n    \"refreshToken\": \"eyJraWQiOiIuLi4iLCJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiJ9...\",\n    \"tokenType\": \"Bearer\",\n    \"expiresIn\": 900\n}"
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"description": "The external auth service geo-post-api trusts (issues the RS256 JWTs `middlewares.RequireAuth()` verifies). It is a separate system, not part of this repo - this folder exists purely so the collection is self-sufficient for testing. geo-post-api never calls it at request time.\n\nRun **LogIn(GetToken)** first - its test script saves `accessToken`/`refreshToken` from the response into the `TOKEN`/`REFRESH_TOKEN` collection variables automatically."
		},
